  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a November 5, 2026 official statement, Attorney General Todd Blanche said the Department of Justice would launch a Super Intelligence Task Force to partner with SI Force Chair Jay Clayton and ensure critical SI technologies are not manipulated by bad actors. The same statement said DOJ would continue identifying and prosecuting individuals whose use of SI violates the law, including by targeting taxpayers, critical infrastructure, or national security. In reported remarks, Blanche said he did not need more AI laws or regulation right now and that “we’re prosecutors, not regulators,” so “we’re not going to try to regulate AI.” In the supplied evidence, Blanche also said “we can’t lose the AI race to China” and said theft of intellectual property involving cutting-edge super intelligence technology was taken extremely seriously.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s7"
   ],
